ion":"A California pawn shop is opposing a trademark application for \"Gold Digger\" filed by a company connected to Jordan Hudson, then-companion of Bill Belichick.","published":"2026-11-18T00:07:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/50514442/pawn-shop-fights-gold-digger-trademark-filed-hudson","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Anthony Olivieri","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma coach Venables shouts out Love's after Buc-ee's comment","description":"Venables showed love Sunday to Buc-ee's -- which is owned by an alumnus of the Sooners' next opponent, Texas A&M. So on Tuesday the coach repped the Oklahoma-based Love's.","published":"2026-11-17T22:23:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50513199/oklahoma-brent-venables-loves-travel-stop","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-17T21:26:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"North Texas QB Tayven Jackson out with upper-body injury","description":"North Texas senior quarterback Tayven Jackson, who is sixth in the FBS with 3,005 passing yards, will miss at least the next two games with an upper-body injury.","published":"2026-11-17T20:53:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50513204/north-texas-qb-tayven-jackson-upper-body-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4871079/boubacar-traore","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boubacar_Traore_(American_football)"},"pick":{"pick":25,"round":1,"team":"PHI","via":"JAX","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Boubacar Traore (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boubacar_Traore_(American_football)","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-17T20:11:49Z","intro":"Boubacar Traore (born October 24, 2004) is an American college football defensive end for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at Notre Dame in 2023, Traore played in five games, totaling one sack and a forced fumble. He became a starter in 2024 after an injury to Jordan Botelho and recorded a 34-yard interception return touchdown against Purdue in the third game of the season. He was the team's leader in sacks (3) and tackles-for-loss (5) before suffering a season-ending knee injury in the fifth game of the season."}]}}